  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shri Krishna vs State Of U.P. on 29 January, 2020 Author: Dinesh Kumar Singh Bench: Dinesh Kumar Singh High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ? Court No. - 13 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 363 of 2008 Revisionist :- Shri Krishna Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Revisionist :- M.K. Shukla Counsel for Opposite Party :- Govt.Advocate Hon'ble Dinesh Kumar Singh,J. 1.",
    "facts": "4.The complainant, Food Inspector, on 24th October, 1985, at around 11.00 a.m., during the course of inspection, got suspicion that food item (Dalmoth) being sold by the revisionist was adulterated; he bought 750 gram Dalmoth from the revisionist, and after preparing the samples, sent the samples for examination to the Public Analyst; the samples sent for examination was found to be wanting the parameters prescribed under the PFA Act. 5. Counsel for the revisionist states that the incident is of 1985; the revisionist had undergone 47 days imprisonment.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel places reliance on judgment of the Supreme Court in Nand Lal v. State of Uttarakhand and others, 2010 (4) SCC 562, and states that after considering the age of the appellant, and taking into account the fact that the incident was very old, the Supreme Court reduced the sentence to the period already undergone by the appellant in that case.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel places reliance on judgment of the Supreme Court in Nand Lal v. State of Uttarakhand and others, 2010 (4) SCC 562, and states that after considering the age of the appellant, and taking into account the fact that the incident was very old, the Supreme Court reduced the sentence to the period already undergone by the appellant in that case.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
